      "fallback_used": false,
      "fallback_attempts": [],
      "attempt_count": 1,
      "asr_text": "For seven nights, at midnight, I lifted his latch. You should have seen my patience. I eased the door open so slowly he never stirred. Then let one thin ray escape my lantern. The eye was always closed, so I could do nothing. You understand, I hated the eye, not the man. Each morning, I kindly asked how he had slept. On the eighth night, I nearly laughed at my cleverness. Then my thumb slipped against the lantern's fastenings.",
